gzip 1.2.4's deflate, for the port's resource packs (port/host/pack.c,
docs/PORT.md "Resource packs").

deflate.c, trees.c, bits.c, gzip.h, tailor.h, lzw.h, crypt.h and COPYING are
from gzip-1.2.4.tar.gz (https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gzip/gzip-1.2.4.tar.gz, sha256
1ca41818a23c9c59ef1d5e1d00c0d5eaa2285d931c0fb059637d7c0cc02ad967), unchanged.
Copyright (C) 1992-1993 Jean-loup Gailly; GNU General Public License, version
2 or (at your option) any later version (COPYING).

gzip124.c and gzip124.h are the port's: they stand in for gzip.c, zip.c and
util.c, so that the deflate reads and writes memory.  gzip124_names.h renames
gzip's global names (CMake includes it before each of these files), which
clash with the game's own gzip inflate (blastcorps/src/gzip_*.inc.c).  Same
license.

Why gzip's own: the ROM's gzip members were made by gzip 1.2.4 at -6 (docs/
ASSETS.md, "gzip"), and only its deflate gives back their bytes; zlib's
differs in 86 of each ROM's 738 members.
